  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "L1 gold contexts uniformly report absolute oral bioavailability values or qualitative outcomes consistent with F >= 20% in humans for diverse lipophilic, basic, and heteroaromatic molecules; propylthiouracil, a thiourea-containing drug, has F 77 ± 13% (C02), and melperone, vernakalant, suvorexant, levofloxacin, BI 425809, phytoene, hyperforin, and pentazocine-in-cirrhosis all support F >= 20% (C01,C05,C14,C08,C11,C13,C07,C06,C04,C10,C12,C03,C09). None provides affirmative evidence of F < 20%.",
