      "claim": "L3 etamicastat, a cyclic-thiourea-containing molecule, shows measurable oral AUC after 200 mg with minimal food effect (C32,C42), supporting oral absorption and systemic exposure of thiourea-containing scaffolds.",
      "card_ids": ["C32","C42"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 nepicastat, a close cyclic-thiourea analog, is highly permeable across Caco-2 and MDCK-II monolayers (Papp ~5.3-5.4 × 10^-5 cm/s; C89,C91,C119,C81,C129); lorcaserin, a small lipophilic basic chloroarene, is highly permeable with no P-gp substrate behavior (C94,C111,C100,C113,C127,C86,C126); domperidone absorption is virtually complete (C98,C128,C85); indapamide is 100% absorbed (C99); UC-781 is high permeability (C101). This supports favorable intestinal absorption for the query's lipophilic basic heteroaromatic scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C89","C91","C119","C81","C129","C94","C111","C100","C113","C127","C86","C126","C98","C128","C85","C99","C101"]
    },
