  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No matched IV comparator is available for the query or the L3/L6 reference records, so F cannot be quantified from exposure or permeability data.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability data are available; L6 records are for reference molecules with partial structural overlap.",
    "Aqueous solubility of the query is not experimentally measured; high logP/logD suggests a possible dissolution limitation, but BCS II analogs in L4 show high permeability.",
    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data are available; L5 records are for reference molecules, not the query.",
    "L1 contexts are training references rather than query-specific measurements; transfer is structural/mechanistic rather than direct."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds mixed hepatic clearance/metabolic stability evidence: lorcaserin-like low HLM CLint supports the lipophilic basic chloroarene core, while thiouracil and prenylated-flavonoid records raise a metabolic-lability concern that is not query-specific and is outweighed by human F of propylthiouracil (77%) and high permeability of cyclic thiourea analogs. Combined with uniformly high L1 gold-context F values and L3-L5 absorption/permeability/efflux evidence, F >= 20% remains better supported. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence due to unquantified first-pass metabolism and solubility."
}

